- [ ] `translate_document.py` wrapper correctly stages source file to GCS per the existing backend's expected convention, independent of IPRU NexGen's own `STORAGE_BACKEND` setting.
- [ ] Translated result is pulled back into IPRU NexGen's own storage and produces a standard `generated_file` record.
- [ ] Tool correctly declines for freeform pasted-text translation requests (handles those as plain chat instead).
- [ ] Registered in `tool_registry.py`; frontend `toolsConfig.ts` entry confirmed enabled.
- [ ] Translated file appears under the correct chat bubble with working Download (and Preview/Edit if type-appropriate) using Phase 3's existing UI, including 24h expiry and "Expired" state.
- [ ] Existing translate backend itself untouched.

Please confirm the two flagged defaults (independent GCS staging regardless of `STORAGE_BACKEND`; synchronous blocking call) before finalizing, and confirm whether translated PDFs should be download-only or if this tool should wait on Phase 4 for full parity.
